@WanderingDudeBM
This is the function with the one line commented out. Paste into a text editor, save as a *.js file, include as a plugin.
Code:
Scene_Map.prototype.updateMainMultiply = function() {
    if (this.isFastForward()) {
//        this.cancelMessageWait();
        this.updateMain();
    }
    this.updateMain();
};

@WanderingDudeBM
Just as a note if you start doing any classes or tutorials - RPG Maker uses JavaScript, not Java. Similar names, two different programming languages.
That's a good point. I'll bear that in mind.
